<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>6.5.1: Undoing FOIL</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01658</md:content-id>
    <md:title>6.5.1: Undoing FOIL</md:title>
    <md:uuid>69700cfc-cf88-43f4-8e91-e0425f39f186</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>In this unit, remember to double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge, if needed.</para>
<para>We are going to factor the trinomial \(q^2 + 10q + 24\) by reversing the process of FOIL.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Find all the different combinations of factors of \(24\). One example is provided in the table.</para>
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis> Factors of 24</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> Sum of factors</emphasis></entry></row>
      <row>
          <entry><para>\(1, 24\)</para></entry>
          <entry><para>\(1 + 24 = 25\)</para></entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry> </entry>
          <entry> </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody></tgroup></table>
    
    
  
  <para>Write down your answers. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    
    <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
      <tgroup cols="2"><tbody><row>
          <entry><emphasis> Factors of 24</emphasis></entry><entry><emphasis> Sum of factors</emphasis></entry></row>
      <row>
        <entry><para>\(1\), \(24\)</para></entry>
        <entry><para>\(1 + 24 = 25\)</para></entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry><para>\(2\), \(12\)</para></entry>
        <entry><para>\(2 + 12 = 14\)</para></entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry><para>\(3\), \(8\)</para></entry>
        <entry><para>\(3 + 8 = 11\)</para></entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry><para>\(4\), \(6\)</para></entry>
        <entry><para>\(4 + 6 = 10\)</para></entry>
      </row>
    </tbody></tgroup></table>
  
  

</solution></exercise>
</example>
<para>We’re going to look at these factors to see which of them would fit in the boxes and multiply to make the trinomial \(q^2 + 10q + 24\) that we started with in the beginning.</para>
<para>\((q+\square)(q+\square)\)</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Which pair of factors fits the situation? What is the factored expression?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para>\(4\), \(6\); \((q + 4)(q + 6)\)</para>
    
    <para>So, by undoing FOIL, we found that the trinomial \(q^2 + 10q + 24\) factors to the expression \((q + 4)(q + 6)\).</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
